Game Rules:
- Users opt in to compete in a PGA Tournament. 
- All opted in users select 3 golfers per tournament to complete their Team. 
- No golfer can be selected by more than 1 user, per tournament. 
- Lowest combined Team score wins (scores from all 3 golfers count towards the Team score)
- If a player has a "TotalScore" value of “null” after 2 rounds, then their tournament score should follow these rules. 

Take the "TotalStrokes" value for this player and multiply by 2, then subtract the "Par" value after multiplying it by 4. For example, for a player with a “TotalScore” of “null”, a “TotalStrokes” of 138, and a “Par” of 70, their score should be (138x2)-(70x4)‎ = -4. This player’s final score will count as -4 for the user whose team includes this player. 

- After tournament completion, losing teams owe the winning team $1 per stroke their team loses by. 

For example, if there are 4 teams (Team A, Team B, Team C, Team D) and their final scores are as follows:
	
Team A: -4
Team B: -10
Team C: +5
Team D: -1

Then the results should be the following:

Team B wins 

Team A: loses $6
Team B: wins the sum of each loss ($30 total)
Team C: loses $15
Team D: loses $9

- In the event that any Team selects the winner of the golf tournament, the are awarded a bonus bounty following these rules:

    - Highest ranked team member (according to Official World Golf Rankings): $10
    - Second ranked team member: $20
    - Third ranked team member: $30

Bonus bounties are owed by losing team according to these rules:
    - First $10 is owed by the last place team
    - Second $10 is owed by the second to last place team
    - Third $10 is owed by the third to last place team

For example, if Team A includes the tournament winner and this player was the second highest ranking player on their team, then they are awarded $20 by the bottom two teams. If the results are the same as above, then the total results are: 

Team A: loses $6 to Team B, but wins $10 each from Team C and Team D (wins $14)
Team B: wins the sum of each loss ($30 total)
Team C: loses $15 to Team B, pays $10 bonus bounty to Team A
Team D: loses $9 to Team B, pays $10 bonus bounty to Team A